---
// About: the brand page, opened by the floating Good Call mark at the end of the
// tab bar. It reads like the opening pages of a book: no cards, justified text, a
// large initial letter, and chapters marked by a short rule. The disclaimer and
// the privacy notice each have a page of their own.
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import { calls } from '../lib/site';
import { POINTS } from '../lib/game';
import { photos } from '../lib/photos';
import { href } from '../lib/paths';

// Every photographer, once, however many photos of theirs are used.
const credits = [...new Map(Object.values(photos).map((photo) => [photo.by, photo])).values()];
const values = [
  { term: 'Respect', text: "Every scenario starts from everyone's right to be treated with dignity." },
  { term: 'Honesty', text: 'Real situations, plainly told, without shaming anyone for not knowing yet.' },
  { term: 'Calm', text: 'No timers, no leaderboards and no pressure. Learning sticks when you feel safe.' },
  { term: 'Privacy', text: 'No tracking, and nothing shared about you unless you join through your school, college or NGO.' },
  { term: 'Care', text: 'Support is always one tap away, and every course points to charities doing the real work.' },
];
---

<Base
  title="About"
  description="What Good Call is and stands for, how it works, how answers are judged, points, supporting Good Call, and photo credits."
  path="/about/"
  tab="about"
>
  <!-- The logo is already in the bar above, so the page opens like the first page of a
       book. The heading is kept for screen readers. -->
  <h1 class="visually-hidden">About Good Call</h1>

  <div class="longform">
    <div class="prose">
      <p class="drop-cap">
        Good Call is practice for judgement. Each scenario is a moment where the right thing to do is not obvious, or
        is obvious and still hard. You choose, and then you see the reasoning.
      </p>
      <p>
        It starts with consent, because that is where a bad call does the most harm, and because it is for everyone.
        Anyone can misjudge a situation. Anyone can have their own boundary ignored.
      </p>
      <p>
        The work scenarios are for people preparing for job applications and training, especially anyone who does not
        get the extra time or support to prepare. That includes many neurodivergent applicants. Timed tests reward
        people who already know the unwritten rules. Good Call writes the rules down.
      </p>
    </div>

    <section class="page-section" aria-labelledby="values-title">
      <h2 id="values-title">What we stand for</h2>
      <dl class="values">
        {
          values.map((value) => (
            <div>
              <dt>{value.term}</dt>
              <dd>{value.text}</dd>
            </div>
          ))
        }
      </dl>
    </section>

    <section class="page-section" id="how" aria-labelledby="how-title">
      <h2 id="how-title">How it works</h2>
      <ul class="ticks">
        <li>Every course is a book. Open one to see its topics, then start reading.</li>
        <li>No timer. Take as long as you need.</li>
        <li>Every answer comes with its reason, the good ones too.</li>
        <li>One go at each scenario. Once you lock in an answer, it stays.</li>
        <li>Your character plays the main part. Finish a course to unlock something new for them to wear.</li>
        <li>No account needed. Your progress is saved on this device.</li>
      </ul>
    </section>

    <section class="page-section" aria-labelledby="judged-title">
      <h2 id="judged-title">How answers are judged</h2>
      <p>Real situations are rarely just right or wrong, so there are three verdicts.</p>
      <ul class="verdicts">
        {
          (['best', 'okay', 'risky'] as const).map((call) => (
            <li>
              <span class="verdict-mark" data-call={call} aria-hidden="true">{calls[call].mark}</span>
              <span>
                <b>{calls[call].label}.</b>{' '}
                {call === 'best'
                  ? 'The choice that respects everyone involved and solves the problem.'
                  : call === 'okay'
                    ? 'It avoids the worst outcome but leaves something undone.'
                    : 'It is likely to hurt someone, or you.'}
              </span>
            </li>
          ))
        }
      </ul>
      <p>Every answer has its reason. The reason is the point, not the score.</p>
    </section>

    <section class="page-section" id="points" aria-labelledby="points-title">
      <h2 id="points-title">About points</h2>
      <p>
        You collect points as you learn: {POINTS.best} for a good call, {POINTS.okay} for one that could be better,{' '}
        {POINTS.risky} for trying, and {POINTS.courseComplete} for finishing a course.
      </p>
      <p>
        We are working on turning the points you collect into real donations to charities connected to each course.
        That is not released yet, so for now points simply add up. Points cannot be bought or sold.
      </p>
      <p>
        Each course links to charities working on what it teaches. They are not partners of Good Call and do not
        endorse it.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section class="page-section donate" id="donate" aria-labelledby="donate-title">
      <h2 id="donate-title">Support Good Call</h2>
      <p>
        Good Call is free, with no account and no tracking, so that anyone can practise the moments that matter. If you
        would like to help us write more courses and reach more schools, colleges and NGOs, you will soon be able to
        donate to Good Call directly.
      </p>
      <button type="button" class="btn gold block" aria-disabled="true" aria-describedby="donate-note">Donate to Good Call</button>
      <p class="fine" id="donate-note">Donations are opening soon.</p>
    </section>

    {
      credits.length > 0 && (
        <details class="credits-fold">
          <summary>Photo credits</summary>
          <p>
            Photos are from <a href="https://unsplash.com/">Unsplash</a>, used under the{' '}
            <a href="https://unsplash.com/license">Unsplash Licence</a>. Thank you to:
          </p>
          <ul class="credits">
            {credits.map((photo) => (
              <li>
                <a href={photo.page} target="_blank" rel="noopener">
                  {photo.by}
                </a>
              </li>
            ))}
          </ul>
          <p class="fine">Book covers and characters are drawn for Good Call.</p>
        </details>
      )
    }

    <p class="fine">
      Please read the <a href={href('/disclaimer/')}>disclaimer</a> and the{' '}
      <a href={href('/privacy/')}>privacy notice</a> before you use Good Call.
    </p>
  </div>
</Base>
